<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Run A — FALLBACK variant of TestMod_Change's patches.
       Selected by `run_test.sh` in expect-fallback mode; the runner copies this to
       Patches/Change.xml before the Run A (cold, provenance-capture) launch.

       Why this file exists:
         The default change fixtures (Change_RunA.xml / Change_RunB.xml) keep ALL
         container ops in the UNCHANGED static mod, so SubDocExpander never trips its
         changed-mod fallback and the real sub-doc recompute is exercised. To prove the
         OTHER branch — the conservative full-rebuild fallback — the CHANGED mod itself
         must own a container op. This variant gives joof.testharness.change a
         PatchOperationSequence.

       How the fallback is armed (verified against SubDocExpander.Expand):
         The fallback fires when, for some BASELINE-graph patch edge,
         changedModIds.Contains(edge.SourceMod) AND edge.PatchId is a container child
         ("...operations[N]" => PatchOperationSequence). So the sequence must be present
         on BOTH runs: Run A (this file) so its child ops are captured into
         DependencyGraph.json as joof.testharness.change#N.operations[M] edges, and Run B
         (Change_RunB_Fallback.xml) which EDITS a value inside it so the patch file hash
         changes and the mod lands in LastChangedMods. Both conditions then hold on Run B
         and SubDocExpander returns needsFullRebuild=true.

         Each sequence child is a PatchOperationAdd (a PatchOperationPathed), so it gets an
         ".operations[N]" id and an edge with modified nodes; the parent sequence is not
         pathed and produces no edge of its own. The child xpaths target real defs
         (TC_SeqTarget, TC_Identity) that exist on Run A so the ops succeed and the edges
         are captured.

       Note this fixture intentionally does NOT also widen the wildcard or flip the
       conditional — the static mod still owns those, but on a fallback load the recompute
       declines entirely (full rebuild is authoritative), so only the sequence-ownership
       matters for the path under test. -->

  <!-- The container op owned by the CHANGED mod: a 2-op sequence touching TC_SeqTarget
       then TC_Identity. Present (and successfully matching) on Run A so its children are
       recorded as container-child edges in the baseline graph. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
    <operations>
      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="TC_SeqTarget"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <changeSeqTag>run-a</changeSeqTag>
        </value>
      </li>
      <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="TC_Identity"]</xpath>
        <value>
          <changeSeqTag>run-a</changeSeqTag>
        </value>
      </li>
    </operations>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
